# Who reviews what, so a change to a rule cannot merge without the person who owns it.
#
# The rule set is the reason this file exists. `rules/` is where the kit states what it
# refuses and why — a cap value, a blocking verdict, a threshold — and a change there
# changes every consumer's behaviour without touching a line of their code. Nothing
# declared an owner for it, so such a change was reviewable by whoever happened to look.
#
# Paths are matched last-wins, GitHub-gitignore style. An entry here is a REVIEW
# requirement only when branch protection asks for owner review; without that it is a
# statement of who to ask, which is worth having on its own.

# Everything, unless a later line is more specific.
*                                   @paulohenriquevn

# The contracts. A change here is a change to what every consumer is held to.
/rules/                             @paulohenriquevn
/skills/_kit-rules/                 @paulohenriquevn

# The gates that enforce them, and the hook library they run through.
/mechanisms/gates/                  @paulohenriquevn
/hooks/                             @paulohenriquevn
/squad/                             @paulohenriquevn

# How the kit reaches a consumer's disk. A defect here lands in every install.
/mechanisms/distribution/           @paulohenriquevn

# The pipeline that decides whether any of the above is green.
/.github/                           @paulohenriquevn
